<title>USA: NYMEX seat sells for record $600,000.</title>
<headline>NYMEX seat sells for record $600,000.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Mercantile Exchange (NYMEX) said Wednesday that one of its seats sold at a record $600,000, the second highest for any seat on a U.S. futures exchange.</p>
<p>A seat on the Chicago Board of Trade most recently sold for $700,000 and one on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange for $525,000, the NYMEX said in a press release.</p>
<p>A NYMEX seat changed hands in December for $585,000, the previous record-high.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
